WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:01.930
- Doesn't smell horrible.

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:03.830
Okay, there's the smell.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.365
Yup that's pungent.

00:00:05.365 --> 00:00:09.160
(light upbeat music)

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.710
Hi, I'm Alix, and I love
cooking and history.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.470
Throughout history there have been

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.780
hundreds of food trends
that have come and gone.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.570
Today, I'm gonna be trying
out one of these recipes

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.500
and seeing if it's edible.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.160
Okay, Oyster and Chicken Pie.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.473
(light upbeat music)

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.130
It's very vague, very under-seasoned,

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:40.040
seems a little random and weird.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.700
I feel like when you see a
pie, like a chicken-pot-pie,

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.560
it's really like, comforting
and warm and inviting.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.130
If I dove into this pie,
I'd be very disappointed.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.860
I guess I'm just gonna go line by line.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.210
The first thing to do
is parboil a chicken.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:58.010
I have no idea how much
chicken I'm suppose to boil,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.920
but I have, I guess,
four breasts right here,

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.390
so we'll go with that.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.910
It immediately turns white.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:08.140
I'm also gonna be hard-boiling
the eggs at the same time.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.116
Nice chicken water in here,

00:01:10.116 --> 00:01:11.480
which is

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.381
pretty fowl.

00:01:12.381 --> 00:01:13.610
(chuckles)

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:15.620
It looks a little like human flesh.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.050
We're off to a good start here.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.460
- [Woman] Wanna hear a fact.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.293
- Yeah sure.

00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:23.270
(smooth jazz music)

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.290
I guess, yeah, actually
oysters are an aphrodisiac,

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:28.657
so I guess everyone's really
horny back in the day.

00:01:28.657 --> 00:01:29.700
(laughs)

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.630
Cool down a little before I peel them,

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:33.450
and then we're gonna cut up this

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.200
partially cooked chicken.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.686
They're looking nice and white.

00:01:37.686 --> 00:01:41.680
(upbeat psychedelic music)

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.040
Over this, place, oh great,
we're at the oyster part.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.950
So, over this chicken,
place one pint of oysters.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.070
Doesn't say to drain
them, but I'm going to,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.482
because I don't know if
I'd wanna pour, like,

00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:57.370
oyster juice all over this chicken.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.170
Product may contain shell fragments.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.778
That seems dangerous.

00:02:01.778 --> 00:02:02.611
Ohhhh.

00:02:02.611 --> 00:02:06.140
Okay I'm just gonna air
it out for a second.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.210
I'm not even exaggerating,
that is so strong.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.081
Okay.

00:02:10.081 --> 00:02:13.248
(upbeat, jazzy music)

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.986
Alright, next.

00:02:16.986 --> 00:02:18.660
If I can make it.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.750
Add two hard-boiled eggs,
cut into small pieces.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.070
Whoever invented this recipe was like,

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.410
what else can we put on top of this.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.210
But, at least it adds, like,
a nice pop of color, I guess.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.600
A tablespoonful of butter.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.033
Do I just put it in the middle like,

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:35.750
or am I suppose to cut it up?

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.470
Like, there's no internet in these days

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.000
so you would think that they would be

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.200
more detailed with the recipes.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.580
I guess I'm just gonna
just cut the tablespoon up

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.900
and like put it in each third.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.710
Some celery, chopped fine.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.660
What is, some celery?

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.770
I'm guessing it's more than one stock,

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.177
less than three.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:00.760
(upbeat, futuristic music)

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:05.460
We're gonna put this finely
chopped celery on top.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.840
Celery's also very bland,
it's basically water.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.627
(upbeat, jazzy music)

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.660
Yikes, that sounds like a problem.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.620
Yeah, I can't wait to eat this now.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.830
Now, for the seasoning.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.500
They say salt and cayenne,
which is a little bizarre.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.730
I don't wanna get too heavy handed

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:28.870
with this cayenne right now

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.130
but actually, maybe I should.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:33.731
I prefer my mouth be numb
when I bite into this.

00:03:33.731 --> 00:03:34.810
(laughs)

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.990
Yeah, this is actually
the most confusing part.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:40.260
Moisten with flour and and a gill of milk.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.910
Still don't know what a gill of milk is.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.330
I fortunately am not from the
1910s and I have a cellphone,

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:48.010
so I'm gonna look up
what a gill of milk is.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.160
Okay, it's a half a cup.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.987
I guess I'm just gonna go for it.

00:03:50.987 --> 00:03:53.530
So if it's like a half cup, oop, okay.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.080
I'm assuming I have to stir it up

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.740
because I feel like that
would be really bizarre.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:00.090
The milk at the bottom is now like

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.640
the oyster chicken juice water.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.000
Put the puff paste on top.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.610
They don't call it puff pastry,
they call it puff paste.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:09.770
So, I guess in the 1910s

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.570
you had to make your own puff pastry,

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:13.530
but that's like, really fuckin' hard,

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.664
so I will not be doing that.

00:04:15.664 --> 00:04:17.900
(upbeat, modern music)

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.630
Maybe I'll use these scraps

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.020
to make a little design on top.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.000
I feel like I should make an oyster design

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.940
just so people know what
they're getting into.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.240
My oyster kinda looks like a vagina.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.540
So, I'm gonna do an egg wash on this

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.940
even though it doesn't
say that in the recipe.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.550
I want this to at least look pretty

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.470
if it's not going to taste very good.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.880
Also, they didn't tell us
how hot the oven should be.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.030
40 minutes in a moderate oven.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.890
I'm gonna say moderate is, 350.

00:04:45.922 --> 00:04:49.505
(upbeat, futuristic music)

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.320
Alright, so, it's been 40 minutes.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.990
Was the fastest 40 minutes of my life,

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.920
'cause now I have to try this pie.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:07.675
Something I've been dreading.

00:05:07.675 --> 00:05:11.900
(upbeat, optimistic music)

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:12.910
How bad can it be?

00:05:17.136 --> 00:05:18.807
I don't know if I can...

00:05:18.807 --> 00:05:19.640
- [Producer] Oh no.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.890
(mumbling)

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.300
- Oh man, I need someone
else to try this though

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.080
because I don't know if
it's just me, and like,

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.522
I don't really like oysters that much.

00:05:29.522 --> 00:05:32.600
(upbeat, optimistic music)

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.810
- I don't think it's that
bad, I'm kind of into it.

00:05:36.311 --> 00:05:37.607
- Ooooh.

00:05:37.607 --> 00:05:39.280
- The whiff is not promising.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.250
- Yeah, I can't say
that's a pleasant smell.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.590
- I wouldn't go out of my way to eat this,

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:45.000
but I would stop eating it if
I was being polite to someone.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.880
- It's not totally
offensive or undelicious.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.070
Are there potatoes in here?

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:50.930
- It tastes like,

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:53.630
if I was a character in
Spongebob Squarepants,

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:56.660
and I just ingested
like, all of the ocean.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.850
- I don't hate it, I'll say that.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.740
- No, it's not, it's not good.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.510
- Like I don't understand why any

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.250
of this being together was
necessary in any capacity.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.411
- It's a taste that some
people might prefer,

00:06:08.411 --> 00:06:10.370
and we don't flavor shame.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.970
If you didn't have taste
buds, you might think,

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:16.060
hey, this is probably a pretty good pie.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.340
- It's like the ingredients

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:19.090
were held together by Elmer's glue.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.440
- It is a little bit hard
to eat, to be honest.

00:06:22.896 --> 00:06:26.313
(upbeat, acoustic music)

